{
  "$comment": [
    "SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0. printer-bridge/1 messages and what each side makes of them.",
    "Placeholders: \"$walnut\" and \"$oak\" stand for the keys below; {\"$bytes\": n} for an ArrayBuffer of n bytes (transferred with the message); {\"$png\": n} for one of n bytes that begins with the PNG signature (89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A).",
    "requests: a message on the port as the host reads it. expect: \"ignored\" (not a request: no answer), {\"op\": …} (valid, with the fields it must read), or {\"error\": kind} (answered with a failure of that kind; \"re\": the id it carries, null when it has none).",
    "incoming: a message on the port as the client reads it. expect: \"ignored\", or {\"kind\": \"result\" | \"failure\" | \"progress\" | \"event\", …}.",
    "clientEvents (0.3.0): an event on the port as the host reads it (parseClientEvent), before its own checks (granted, the selected printer, a printer that takes writes). expect: \"ignored\", or {\"event\": …, …} with what it must read.",
    "library (0.4.0): a Library answer or event's data as the client reads it. read: \"status\" (library.status's and library.preferences' answers, the library.status event: parseLibraryStatus), \"saved\" (library.save's answer), \"project\" (library.get's, against what was \"asked\" when given), \"open\" (the library.open event). expect: what it reads, or \"refused\" (the client takes it as the host breaking the protocol, or drops the event). Library requests, answers, progress and events name no printer: \"printer\": null.",
    "answers: an operation's result as the client reads it. print.request's (asked with paths and mode): expect the decision, or \"refused\" (not one, or not one that mode answers: the client takes it as the host breaking the protocol, never as a start). queue.add's: expect {\"queued\": boolean} or \"refused\"."
  ],
  "keys": {
    "walnut": "4d2c1e0b7a6f5e4d3c2b1a09f8e7d6c5b4a39281706f5e4d3c2b1a0918273645",
    "oak": "0f1e2d3c4b5a69788796a5b4c3d2e1f00f1e2d3c4b5a69788796a5b4c3d2e1f0"
  },
